[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Planning a Share Portfolio]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.70]Lesson 48 | 第48课
[00:02.50]Planning a share portfolio | 规划股份投资组合
[00:10.35]How does the older investor differ in his approach to investment from the younger investor? | 年长的投资者在投资方式上与年轻的投资者有何不同？
[00:19.17]There is no shortage of tipsters around offering 'get-rich-quick' opportunities. | 四处都不乏提供“快速致富”机会的股票贴士贩子。
[00:24.88]But if you are a serious private investor, leave the Las Vegas mentality to those with money to fritter. | 但如果你是一位认真的个人投资者，就把拉斯维加斯心态留给那些有钱可挥霍的人吧。
[00:32.41]The serious investor needs a proper 'portfolio' --a well-planned selection of investments, with a definite structure and a clear aim. | 认真的投资者需要一个像样的“投资组合”——一份规划周密的投资选择，结构明确、目标清晰。
[00:41.88]But exactly how does a newcomer to the stock market go about achieving that? | 但股市新手究竟该怎么做才能实现这一点呢？
[00:48.15]Well, if you go to five reputable stock brokers and ask them what you should do with your money, | 这样吧，如果你去找五位信誉良好的股票经纪人，问他们你该如何处置你的钱，
[00:54.44]you're likely to get five different answers, | 你很可能会得到五种不同的答案，
[00:57.32]--  even if you give all the relevant information about your age, family, finances and what you want from your investments. | 即使你提供了关于你的年龄、家庭、财务状况以及对投资期望的所有相关信息。
[01:05.48]Moral? There is no one 'right' way to structure a portfolio. | 教训何在？构建投资组合没有唯一“正确”的方法。
[01:10.44]However, there are undoubtedly some wrong ways, and you can be sure that none of our five advisers | 然而，无疑也存在一些错误的方法，而且你可以肯定，我们这五位顾问中
[01:17.23]would have suggested sinking all (or perhaps any) of your money into Periwigs. | 谁也不会建议你把全部（也许连任何一部分）的钱都投进“佩里威格斯”。
[01:23.36]So what should you do? | 那么你该怎么办呢？
[01:25.21]We'll assume that you have sorted out the basics--like mortgages, pensions, insurance and access to sufficient cash reserves. | 我们假定你已经理清了基本问题——比如抵押贷款、养老金、保险以及足够现金储备的获取。
[01:34.00]You should then establish your own individual aims. | 然后你应当确立自己的个人目标。
[01:37.56]These are partly a matter of personal circumstances, partly a matter of psychology. | 这些目标部分取决于个人境况，部分取决于心理因素。
[01:43.67]For instance, if you are older you have less time to recover from any major losses, and you may well wish to boost your pension income. | 比方说，如果你年事已高，你从重大损失中恢复的时间就较少，而且你可能很想增加自己的养老金收入。
[01:53.09]So preserving your capital and generating extra income are your main priorities. | 因此，保住本金并获得额外收入就是你的首要目标。
[01:59.36]In this case, you'd probably construct a portfolio with some shares (but not high risk ones), along with gilts, cash deposits, | 在这种情况下，你可能会构建一个包含一些股票（但不是高风险股）、金边债券、现金存款，
[02:09.00]and perhaps convertibles or the income shares of split capital investment trusts. | 或许还有可转换债券或分拆资本投资信托收益股的投资组合。
[02:15.11]If you are younger, and in a solid financial position, | 如果你比较年轻，而且财务状况稳固，
[02:19.49]you may decide to take an aggressive approach--but only if you're blessed with a sanguine disposition and won't suffer sleepless nights over share prices. | 你可能会决定采取激进的做法——但前提是你天生乐观开朗，不会因股价波动而夜不能寐。
[02:29.68]If you recognize yourself in this description, | 如果你发现自己符合这番描述，
[02:32.72]you might include a couple of heady growth stocks in your portfolio, alongside your more pedestrian investments. | 你或许可以在更平稳的投资之外，把几只令人亢奋的成长股纳入自己的投资组合。
[02:40.96]Once you have decided on your investment aims you can then decide where to put your money. | 一旦确定了投资目标，你就可以决定把钱投向何处。
[02:47.65]The golden rule here is spread your risk--if you put all of your money into Periwigs International, | 这里的黄金法则是分散风险——如果你把所有的钱都投进“佩里威格斯国际”，
[02:55.44]you're setting yourself up as a hostage to fortune. | 你就是在把自己置于命运的劫持之下。
